WEBVTT

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.650
Takagi Sakuya, eh?

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:08.820
From what I see in his match with Yukichi,

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.900
he seems like an all-rounder who's devoted 
to fundamentals and has few blind spots.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:17.400
<i>That's a rather casual way 
of deciding who serves.</i>

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:18.660
Okay, bottom.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:19.910
Top it is.

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:21.660
My serve.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:24.460
<i>He didn't even check. He already knew.</i>

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:26.920
<i>Regardless, I have to win.</i>

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:28.420
Good luck.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:09.620
It's amazing.

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:12.200
Bro's made it to the top eight now.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:13.490
Yeah.

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:15.040
His first round was one thing,

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:17.280
but his second round was 
against Ide, after all.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:21.180
Ide was among the top eight players at

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:22.960
the All-Japan Indoor Invitational,

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:25.690
and he's at a level where even 
national players watch out for him.

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:27.450
He isn't someone you can beat by a fluke.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:30.820
It's been only two years 
since he started tennis.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:34.340
I've never seen an athlete improve so rapidly.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:37.460
That shows how hard Maruo has worked.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:45.350
He thoroughly practiced the fundamentals, 
which everyone hates doing.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:48.900
And the biggest reason for his growth

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:52.480
is how he never stopped thinking about tennis.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:57.070
An old philosopher once said that 
man is a "thinking reed."

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:59.660
What? Feet can think?

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:04.130
"Ashi" as in "reed," not "foot." You know, 
the plant that's similar to silver grass.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:09.120
It means that people are weak,
but they have the ability to think.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:13.110
In other words, thinking is 
mankind's greatest weapon.

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:17.620
Both while training and during matches, 
Maruo has always put that into practice.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.010
Thinking, huh?

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:24.090
Those notebooks are proof of the 
amount of effort Maruo has put in.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:29.550
Today he's facing Takagi, who was in the 
top sixteen in last year's All-Japan Junior.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.520
And I lost to him!

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:35.910
Maruo's goal is to win the All-Japan Junior.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:40.360
That means, regardless of who his 
opponent is, he has to win.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:43.460
Maruo doesn't have a lot of experience.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.720
Even if he doesn't win today,

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:48.740
he needs to gain experience 
by facing a lot of strong players,

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:52.370
so he can win the national 
tournament in three months.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:55.230
He should be careful during this match.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:57.370
Takagi's a tough one to play against.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:00.380
He's a <i>really</i> nasty opponent.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:05.940
Yes!

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.910
<i>As expected from a fourth seed.</i>

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.470
<i>His hits are deep and seem
to stretch away from my reach.</i>

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:12.600
<i>But...</i>

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.310
<i>We're still just warming up!</i>

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:18.820
<i>Why is he hitting so hard?</i>

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:24.000
<i>He really is a strange person.</i>

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:32.120
Psychological Warfare and Self-Control

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:43.060
<i>My opponent is the rising star 
everyone's eyes are on.</i>

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:47.420
<i>But there's a reason I can't 
possibly lose this match.</i>

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.340
<i>You were always, always</i>

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:53.120
<i>ahead of me, Nabae.</i>

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:56.980
<i>That's why, if you ran ten kilometers,</i>

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:58.680
<i>I would run fifteen.</i>

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:01.480
<i>I thought if I did that, 
I could beat you one day.</i>

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:05.340
<i>If he practiced his forehand for three hours,</i>

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.610
<i>I made sure to practice longer than that.</i>

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:10.120
<i>As a result, I got stronger.</i>

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:13.820
<i>But I couldn't defeat Nabae.</i>

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.560
<i>That's why I always did more.</i>

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:28.860
Hey.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:31.740
It's already late. Let's call it a night.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:32.890
No way.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.890
Don't run away just because it's
not going your way anymore.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:36.910
What?

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:40.420
You're afraid you'll lose to me 
for the first time, aren't you?

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:42.520
That's not it.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:44.990
It's almost midnight.

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:47.620
We've got practice tomorrow, too.

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:49.410
We can finish this another time.

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:53.180
Even an official match gets 
postponed once the sun goes down.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:55.150
This isn't an official match!

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:56.750
It's a showdown between you and me!

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:59.880
I'm saying I won't accept all that!

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.400
What's with you today?

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:05.670
Do you want to win that badly?

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:07.990
Don't patronize me!

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:10.270
<i>That's right.</i>

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:14.470
<i>I don't care if it's lame or distasteful.
I want to beat you just once!</i>

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:17.710
Fine.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:20.760
If you're gonna do this, 
you better give it your all.

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:23.420
I know.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:26.110
4-3. Here it comes!

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:33.950
<i>I'll reflect on my actions </i>after<i> I win.</i>

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:38.210
<i>If I can't win at least once, 
I can't move forward!</i>

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.740
Best of three set match.

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:43.630
Takagi to serve.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:52.970
<i>That's fast!</i>

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:57.820
<i>He has good control on his backhand, too.</i>

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:03.360
15-love.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:07.120
<i>His basic shots like serves and 
ground strokes are high-level.</i>

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:12.870
<i>This isn't the time to think
about how strange he is.</i>

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:20.370
Yeah!

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:21.500
30-love.

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:25.410
<i>It's my return game, so being pushed 
back can't be helped, but...</i>

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:28.510
<i>What really bothers me is that</i>

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:33.890
<i>he's been glaring at me this whole time!</i>

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:37.860
<i>He's winning points just fine,
so what's his problem?</i>

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:43.500
E-Excuse me for a second!

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:47.010
Wha—

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:49.240
<i>Why did he...</i>

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:51.310
<i>Why did he serve?!</i>

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:53.720
That serve is invalid.

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:56.870
Maruo's call was made before the shot.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:59.790
See? He's starting to play his tricks.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:01.250
Huh...

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:05.750
<i>Yukichi-kun did say all that stuff about him.</i>

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:10.590
That Takagi guy is really, 
<i>really</i> nasty, so be careful!

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:14.310
That punk was leading 4-2 in the first set,

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:17.720
and he hit an unnecessary and 
unexpected underhand serve!

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:22.230
<i>Maybe this is what Yukichi-kun 
was talking about.</i>

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:32.710
<i>He has a good arm.</i>

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:36.200
<i>Even playing normally, he'd be 
a tough opponent for Maruo.</i>

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:40.850
Game: Takagi. 1-0.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:47.710
<i>He's still glaring.</i>

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:50.300
<i>Seriously, what's with him?</i>

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:53.420
<i>When he's acting this weird, 
I can't help noticing.</i>

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:57.190
<i>But that doesn't change 
what I have to do during play.</i>

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:01.770
<i>Just relax and hit a first serve 
with maximum efficiency,</i>

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:04.320
<i>and hold my serve as quickly as possible.</i>

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:07.200
Fault.

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:09.690
<i>Rushing it threw off my tempo...</i>

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:15.260
Yeah, bring it!

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:17.160
Love-15.

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:20.660
<i>I see. I'm starting to get it.</i>

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:24.280
<i>All these things that seem 
so weird are his strategy.</i>

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:28.540
<i>He's trying to shake me psychologically 
in order to get the upper hand.</i>

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:31.240
<i>I need to stay composed 
at times like these.</i>

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:33.810
<i>I shouldn't let him get to me every time.</i>

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:38.210
<i>Even if I can't do that, 
I'll handle it the same way</i>

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:40.470
<i>I dealt with my pressure two days ago.</i>

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:48.870
15-all.

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:50.110
Yes!

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:52.360
<i>Don't.</i>

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:54.380
<i>I can't fall for his strategy.</i>

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:58.450
<i>It's not like I can score a point 
by glaring back at Takagi-kun.</i>

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:04.970
<i>Was that Takagi-kun tossing the ball back?</i>

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:07.290
H-Hey!

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:10.570
Make sure I'm ready before 
you toss the ball back!

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:11.720
Huh?

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:15.270
Takagi-kun, that was unacceptable.

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:18.410
If I have to call you out 
on your etiquette again,

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:21.430
you will be issued a warning, 
so please be careful.

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:22.950
Okay.

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:31.600
<i>I'm not even running, and my 
heart rate has gone way up.</i>

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:34.070
<i>But Takagi-kun seems completely fine.</i>

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:37.500
<i>And he didn't even get a warning for that,</i>

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:39.390
<i>so I'm the only one hurt by it.</i>

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:43.930
<i>He's strong enough just playing normally.</i>

00:10:43.930 --> 00:10:45.830
<i>Why does he do these things?</i>

00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:50.270
<i>Why is Nabae-kun friends with this guy?</i>

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:54.010
Hmm... I get it now.

00:10:54.430 --> 00:10:56.310
He's pulling all kinds of tricks.

00:10:56.310 --> 00:10:57.370
You see?!

00:10:57.370 --> 00:11:00.180
He's the type who'll do anything to win!

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:04.040
<i>I'm the one who suffers by reacting 
to his attempts to rattle me.</i>

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:06.400
<i>Playing with an increased heart rate</i>

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:08.620
<i>will just tire me out that much faster.</i>

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:10.990
<i>I can't by swayed by that 
psychological warfare.</i>

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:13.690
<i>I should take my time, 
and take a deep breath.</i>

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:18.650
Fifteen seconds.

00:11:22.650 --> 00:11:24.240
30-15.

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:25.950
<i>Yes! That was good.</i>

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:29.330
<i>Don't rush, and focus on control.</i>

00:11:31.610 --> 00:11:33.960
<i>As soon as I have the 
advantage, attack swiftly!</i>

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:37.500
40-15.

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:40.520
<i>And don't make eye contact.</i>

00:11:46.770 --> 00:11:48.730
Game: Maruo. 1-all.

00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:51.540
<i>All right! I can hold.</i>

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:54.140
<i>I'll keep this up and break his serve when I can!</i>

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:56.690
<i>He seems like he'll fall for it, but he doesn't.</i>

00:11:57.180 --> 00:11:59.980
<i>He's good at controlling his emotions, all right.</i>

00:11:59.980 --> 00:12:03.410
<i>Otherwise, there's no way he could've 
beaten Ide in a close match.</i>

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:08.240
<i>Well, I figured from your results 
that you'd be this much of a threat.</i>

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:10.720
<i>But I won't lose this match.</i>

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:14.000
<i>I'm going to face Nabae, no matter what!</i>

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:18.500
There it is!

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:19.970
<i>Underhand serve!</i>

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:32.160
<i>If it's within the rules, 
I'll do whatever it takes!</i>

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:34.140
<i>I will be the one to defeat Nabae!</i>

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:36.480
<i>It should have less speed.</i>

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:40.800
<i>But with that much control,
if I don't hit it back...</i>

00:12:41.710 --> 00:12:44.200
<i>He can't hit it down the line from that stance.</i>

00:12:46.710 --> 00:12:48.080
15-love.

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:52.000
<i>It's faster than what I expected 
from the video I saw.</i>

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.620
<i>And it's a type of shot I've had 
almost zero experience with.</i>

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:56.670
<i>I need to deal with it more quickly.</i>

00:12:58.140 --> 00:13:00.140
<i>He's glaring again.</i>

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:02.090
<i>I should just ignore it,</i>

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:05.170
<i>but when it's his serve, I have 
to match him to some extent,</i>

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:06.270
<i>so it can't be helped.</i>

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:10.470
<i>Regardless, he'll serve within twenty seconds,</i>

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:12.250
<i>so just concentrate on the ball,</i>

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:15.240
<i>and be wary of another 
underhand serve, just in case.</i>

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:20.730
<i>He's taking forever!</i>

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:24.140
<i>His timing is fast!</i>

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:26.720
30-love.

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:30.330
<i>That was a quick serve...</i>

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:31.990
<i>He can do that, too?</i>

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:34.860
Looks like he's practiced 
a lot of different styles.

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:37.770
Quick serves are difficult to pull off.

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:40.170
You have to hit it before 
the toss comes back down.

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:46.200
<i>This is harder than I thought.</i>

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:49.680
<i>He pulls off tricky shots 
without breaking a sweat.</i>

00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:54.100
<i>It's proof that his technique and 
mental strength are well-polished.</i>

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:58.560
<i>More than anything, I can actually 
feel his determination to win.</i>

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:02.320
<i>But that shouldn't mean he 
can get away with anything!</i>

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.320
Takagi Sakuya 
Maruo Eiichiro

00:14:07.670 --> 00:14:09.300
<i>I can't put my finger on it,</i>

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:11.710
<i>but his tennis style is like 
Nabae's in some way.</i>

00:14:11.710 --> 00:14:15.950
<i>He's perfect as target practice to crush 
before playing Nabae in the semifinal.</i>

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:20.090
<i>Even if I can't take the lead right 
now, there's no need to rush.</i>

00:14:20.470 --> 00:14:23.100
<i>If I can just find that 
chance to make my move...</i>

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:25.300
<i>But until then, I have to hold serve.</i>

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:26.800
Time.

00:14:28.350 --> 00:14:30.340
<i>And for that to happen, 
I have to make my first serve!</i>

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:33.220
Yes!

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:34.170
Sorry.

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:36.880
I wasn't ready.

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:37.940
What?!

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:42.980
Maruo, your first serve again, please.

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:46.490
<i>B-But I got an ace!</i>

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:48.970
He got Bro again!

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:53.990
The way he cuts it so close 
tells me he's used to it.

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:56.650
Looks like he'll need something other than

00:14:56.650 --> 00:14:58.820
the mental strength he used to beat Ide.

00:15:00.690 --> 00:15:01.750
<i>Focus.</i>

00:15:07.190 --> 00:15:10.220
They've both held serve all 
the way to the ninth game.

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:12.330
He's doing well.

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:15.760
Even with the technical 
and psychological attacks,

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:19.020
he's managed to keep 
his first serves effective.

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:23.030
I guess it's difficult playing 
against such an erratic player.

00:15:23.410 --> 00:15:24.990
That may be true.

00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:29.820
Maruo's greatest weapon is the ability 
to disrupt the other player's tempo.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:36.410
But against an irregular style like this,
upsetting his tempo is no simple task.

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:40.250
Yes!

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:41.570
Love-30.

00:15:41.570 --> 00:15:43.580
<i>Here it is! My chance to break!</i>

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:45.670
Yeah, Bro! You can do it!

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:47.670
Excuse me.

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:49.880
<i>Huh? What is it this time?</i>

00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:54.550
I feel some discomfort in my leg. 
May I take a medical time-out?

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:57.640
<i>M-Medical time-out?</i>

00:15:57.640 --> 00:15:59.020
Again...

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:02.230
If I remember correctly, medical 
time-outs are three minutes, right?

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:04.710
Yeah, if a player gets hurt

00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:10.460
or feels ill during a match, and requires 
a doctor's evaluation or first aid,

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:13.410
he can call a medical time-out.

00:16:13.690 --> 00:16:15.630
But three minutes here is...

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:18.160
He should be extra careful.

00:16:18.650 --> 00:16:22.540
A time-out like this can 
change the flow of a match.

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:26.450
<i>Is he okay?</i>

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:29.300
<i>He seemed completely fine a moment ago.</i>

00:16:41.010 --> 00:16:43.020
Game: Takagi. 5-4.

00:16:44.300 --> 00:16:45.470
Yeah!

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:48.360
He changed the flow of the match.

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:50.520
Bro...

00:16:50.520 --> 00:16:52.820
That was his chance to break serve!

00:16:58.020 --> 00:17:01.230
<i>It seems like his leg is totally fine!</i>

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:02.610
<i>So he faked it?</i>

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:06.330
<i>Even if not, I can only assume 
he was exaggerating it.</i>

00:17:07.140 --> 00:17:09.540
<i>Don't tell me he utilized the medical time-out</i>

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:11.740
<i>to escape the disadvantage he was in?</i>

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:14.270
<i>Who would do that?</i>

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:18.980
<i>At this point, it's kind of incredible.</i>

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:21.710
<i>He's already a strong player,</i>

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:24.840
<i>but he takes advantage of 
the rules in unbelievable ways.</i>

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:27.610
<i>How does he think up these things?</i>

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:30.280
<i>Even once you come up with them,</i>

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:33.380
<i>how do you pull it off without 
disrupting your own tempo?</i>

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:38.120
<i>Does that mean he has as many tricks 
as Nabae-kun does, in a different way?</i>

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:40.770
<i>No, this isn't the time to be impressed.</i>

00:17:40.770 --> 00:17:43.160
<i>The question is how to deal with it.</i>

00:17:43.470 --> 00:17:44.410
Time.

00:17:45.050 --> 00:17:45.910
<i>All right...</i>

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:50.420
<i>If Takagi-kun is going to use his tricks 
against me outside the game,</i>

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:54.210
<i>I'll fight back with my own 
tricks within the game!</i>

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:01.180
<i>After a sliding slice comes a bouncing spin!</i>

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:08.130
<i>I'll combine different hits, 
speeds, courses, and styles</i>

00:18:08.130 --> 00:18:11.370
<i>so he can't predict where or 
what kind of ball is coming.</i>

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:17.700
<i>Changing the pace theoretically 
has infinite attack patterns!</i>

00:18:18.350 --> 00:18:19.700
15-love.

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:20.790
Yes!

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:22.430
<i>The opponent is the opponent.</i>

00:18:22.430 --> 00:18:23.560
<i>I am myself.</i>

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:25.790
<i>I just have to fight using my own strengths.</i>

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:29.500
<i>Sliding and bouncing... 
Talk about annoying shots.</i>

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:34.390
Game: Maruo. 5-all.

00:18:34.390 --> 00:18:36.010
<i>Yes! I held!</i>

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:38.370
If he doesn't break next...

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:41.350
It might not be that easy to do.

00:18:41.900 --> 00:18:44.690
But with the mental strength 
he had when he beat Ide...

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:49.210
It may have been mental strength, 
but it was a battle against his own pressure.

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:53.020
This, on the other hand, is a battle
against his own self-control.

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:55.360
They're similar, but not the same,

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:58.530
so it might be difficult for 
the inexperienced Maruo.

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:06.160
30-40.

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:09.950
<i>That sound just now... 
I thought he moved up.</i>

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:12.530
Ugh, again!

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:14.710
Endure it, Maruo.

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:18.860
Yes!

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:21.120
Game: Maruo. 6-all.

00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:22.810
Tiebreaker.

00:19:23.230 --> 00:19:24.820
<i>I managed to hold.</i>

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:28.340
He ended up in a tiebreaker.

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:31.770
He's endured that erratic style well thus far.

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:34.360
But this is where it gets crucial.

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:39.470
<i>Even if it's 6-all, I've won more points so far.</i>

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:42.880
<i>I have the upper hand if it's 
a tiebreaker to seven points.</i>

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:45.690
<i>Concentrate only on my own play!</i>

00:19:58.180 --> 00:20:00.410
Now the score is 6-3.

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:01.680
It's over.

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:06.970
If you depend on tricks like 
trying to fool your opponents

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:11.930
and break their concentration, 
your tennis will never improve.

00:20:11.930 --> 00:20:12.850
Next!

00:20:13.380 --> 00:20:16.110
We've played nine sets already. Just stop this.

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:20.310
Don't try to run away from 
a match by lecturing me!

00:20:20.850 --> 00:20:24.030
I'm finally getting the hang of it!

00:20:32.770 --> 00:20:35.750
If you're tired, just lose and 
you'll feel a lot better.

00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:40.510
<i>I've practiced more than 
you have, if nothing else.</i>

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:43.240
<i>If it's a battle of endurance, 
I have a chance to win.</i>

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:47.760
Just so you know, tennis can't 
be won on stamina alone.

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:14.790
I won...

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:16.890
I beat

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:19.550
Nabae!

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:23.100
Yes!

00:21:23.100 --> 00:21:24.490
4-3, Maruo.

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:29.220
Takagi Sakuya
Maruo Eiichiro

00:21:25.210 --> 00:21:27.290
<i>If we're neck-and-neck 
and I take the first set,</i>

00:21:27.290 --> 00:21:29.220
<i>I'll immediately have the upper hand.</i>

00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:33.940
<i>I need this set in order to 
corner him in the second set.</i>

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:36.620
<i>I have to break somehow!</i>

00:21:38.390 --> 00:21:42.440
<i>After I defeated Nabae that day, 
I undoubtedly moved forward.</i>

00:21:43.010 --> 00:21:44.810
<i>In order to move ahead even more,</i>

00:21:44.810 --> 00:21:47.110
<i>I'll beat Nabae in this tournament, too!</i>

00:21:47.580 --> 00:21:49.700
<i>I'm different from you.</i>

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:52.560
<i>You don't know how miserable 
it feels not to be able to win!</i>

00:21:52.560 --> 00:21:55.220
<i>That's why I'll do whatever it takes!</i>

00:21:58.590 --> 00:21:59.880
<i>Good serve!</i>

00:22:03.970 --> 00:22:05.550
<i>A drop shot here?!</i>

00:22:12.230 --> 00:22:15.140
<i>He can go for the left, right, or above...</i>

00:22:15.140 --> 00:22:16.810
<i>Or maybe he'll hit it low this time?</i>

00:22:20.220 --> 00:22:21.190
<i>Right at me?!</i>

00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:24.440
<i>Why did he go for such a risky shot?!</i>

00:22:26.600 --> 00:22:27.580
<i>Oh, no!</i>

00:24:00.020 --> 00:24:25.040
Next Time

00:24:00.410 --> 00:24:03.000
It's the rules that decide 
good and evil on the court.

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:06.500
Takagi-kun is just playing with his own style.

00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:09.590
I just have to play with my own style, too!

00:24:09.590 --> 00:24:11.630
What's with that face?

00:24:11.630 --> 00:24:13.400
If you think you can do it, just try!

00:24:13.400 --> 00:24:16.110
I've come this far. All I have to do 
now is crush you in one blow!

00:24:16.110 --> 00:24:18.910
I don't know what Nabae sees in this guy,

00:24:18.910 --> 00:24:20.680
but I refuse to accept it!

00:24:21.190 --> 00:24:22.890
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>,

00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:25.040
Good, Evil, and Rules

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:24.310
"Good, Evil, and Rules."

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:30.970
End
